From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cli: bound live observability query load

Each WebUI session independently refreshed live topology every two seconds.
One topology response expanded into repeated get_network and get_sta commands,
and parallel browser sessions multiplied that work. The controller and CLI
also printed every command, station lookup, and complete topology payload to
both journald and syslog. On a 20-client lab this made logging consume more CPU
than the EasyMesh processes themselves.

Cache successful live projections for less than one UI refresh interval, make
the authoritative STA query stand on its own instead of issuing an unused
topology availability query, and share topology responses across observers.
Retain the last-successful device fallback while never inventing a successful
STA response. Remove hot-path debug and payload dumps, use compact JSON for
published events, and retain all failure diagnostics.

The cache is presentation-only and bounded to 1.5 seconds. It does not alter
controller state, metrics collection, steering, or protocol timing.

Upstream-Status: Pending
